    "explanation": "Herpes simplex virus-2 is the cause of genital herpes.\nMost primary genital herpes simplex virus infections\nare asymptomatic. Lesions evolve from vesicles to\npustules to wet ulcers and heal by crusting. Lesions\noccur on the labia, mons pubis, vaginal mucosa, cervix\nand on the shaft of the penis. Inguinal\nlymphadenopathy, dysuria, and vaginal discharge are\nfrequent complaints. SIMILAR TO PREVIOUS BOARD\nEXAM CONCEPT.",
