    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Henoch-schonlein purpura cause palpable purpuric\nrash, arthritis and intermittent abdominal pain. It is\nthe most common cause of non-thrombocytopenic\npurpura in children. The cause is unknown but it\ntypically follows an URTI.",
