    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0224",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 224,
    "stem": "a 4 y/o female was referred to your clinic\nsecondary to a mass occupying the nasopharyngeal\narea. this is accompanied by congestion, recurrent\nepistaxis and multiple cranial nerve palsies. Patient\nis lethargic with complains of headache and\nrecurrent projectile vomitting. what is the most\nlikely diagnosis for this patient?",
