    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 236,
    "stem": "A 2 day old infant was noted to be cyanotic during\nits hospital stay. Cardiac examination showed 3-4/6\nsystolic murmur with prominent second heart\nsound without any splitting. 12LECG - LVH, CXR:\ndecrease pulmonary markings with a normal\ncardiac size without displacement. which of the\nfollowing medications is needed to administer ?",
