    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 351,
    "stem": "A 3 year old boy presents at the ER with a 3 day\nhistory of abdominal pain and difficulty walking.\nAbnormal findings include BP of 120/80, diffuse\nabdominal tenderness, purpuric rash of the legs\nand ankles, and swelling and tenderness over the\nankles. The most likely diagnosis is:",
