    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0483",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 483,
    "stem": "The mother of Madeen, a 6-day old infant, has\ndeveloped multiple vesicular lesions throughout\nher body. Which of the following is the correct\nmanagement?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Isolate the infant from the mother."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Administer acyclovir to the infant."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Administer varicella-zoster immunoglobulin to\nthe infant."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Continue regular well-baby care for the infant."
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "SIMILAR TO PREVIOUS BOARD EXAM\nCONCEPT/PRINCIPLE This is a case of varicella in a\nnew postpartum mother. VZIG is only administered to\nthe infant immediately if the mother had the onset of\nvaricella within 5 days prior to delivery and 2 days\nafter delivery. This is already a 6-day old infant so\nVZIG and isolation are not necessary. Acyclovir is\ngiven only to treat infants with lesions.",
