    "stem": "Andy, a 3-day old infant was noted to have\nprogressively deepening cyanosis since birth.\nWhich of the following congenital cardiac\nmalformations is most likely responsible for her\ncyanosis?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Transposition of great arteries"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Tetralogy of Fallot"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Tricuspid atresia"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Total anomalous pulmonary venous return"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "TGA is the most common cause of early cyanosis in the\nnewborns (unlike TOF which presents with cyanosis\nafter a fews days of life).",
