    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0487",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 487,
    "stem": "Sweet delivered to a term infant which was noted\nto be in respiratory distress shortly after birth. The\ninfant has diminshed breath sounds on the left. A\nCXR was requested revealing a multiloculated mass\nin the left hemithorax. The tip of the NGT placed\nreveals that the stomach is below the diaphragm.\nWhich is the most likely diagnosis?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Congenital diaphragmatic hernia"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Congenital lobar emphysema"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Congenital cystic adenomatoid malformation"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Congenital bronchogenic cysts"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Congenital cystic adenomatoid malformation (CCAM)\narises from an embryonic disruption before 9 wks that\ncauses improper development of bronchioles. Large\nlesions may compress the affected lung and cause\npulmonary hypoplasia.",
