    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0535",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 535,
    "stem": "A 3-year-old boy who is HIV positive is brought for\na routine examination. His diet is appropriate for\nage. His medications include three antiretroviral\ndrugs and trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole for\nPneumocystis carinii prophylaxis. Laboratory\nstudies show:\nHemoglobin 8.6 g/dL\nMean corpuscular hemoglobin 38 pg/cell\nMean corpuscular hemoglobin concentration 30%\nHb/cell\nMean corpuscular volume 101 μm3\nLeukocyte count 5600/mm3\nSegmented neutrophils 60% (many\nhypersegmented)\nBands 3%\nLymphocytes 37%\nRed cell distribution width 21% (N=10–16)\nWhich of the following is most likely to have\nprevented this patient's anemia?",
