    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0549",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 549,
    "stem": "A day old newborn who was under observation in\nthe NICU for temperture instability had a suspected\nseizure. On examination, you note that the patient\nhad wide set eyes, a small mandible and a cleft\npalate. You hear a murmur on auscultation. Chest\nradiograph reveals no apparent thymus. On seeing\nthe results of serum chemistries, you determine\nthat the seizure was probably due to severe\nhypocalcemia. You now suspect a syndrome caused\nby mutant genes in this chromosome:",
