    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0591",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 591,
    "stem": "A 10 year old male was brought to the emergency\nroom due to red-brown urine. Patient had a history\nof sore throat 2 weeks prior. On physical\nexamination, patient was hypertensive, febrile, and\nwith bipedal edema. Urinalysis showed ph 6.0,\nspecific gravity 1.30, albumin 3+, sugar (-), RBC\n40/hpf, WBC 0-2/hpf , RBC casts +. ASO titers were\nelevated. What are the expected biopsy findings\nthat with differentiate it from other causes of acute\nglomerulonephritis?",
