    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 594,
    "stem": "A 17 year old female was rushed to the emergency\nroom due to multiple eythematous papules on the\ntrunk and upper extremities. Patient had was\nrecently given Ciprofloxacin. On examination, there\npapules with an erythematous outer border, an\ninner pale ring, and a dusky purple to necrotic\ncenter noted on the trunk and upper extremities as\nwell as on the oral cavity. What is the most likely\ndiagnosis?",
