    "explanation": "Trisomy 21 (down syndrome) is characetrized by the\nff: hypotonia, flat face, upward and slanted palpebral\nfissures and epicanthic folds, speckled irises\n(Brushfield sports);varying degrees of mental and\ngrowth retardation;dysplasia of the pelvis, cardiac\nmalformations (endocardial cushion defect) and\nsimian crease;short, broad hands, hypoplasia of\nmiddle phalanx of 5th finger, duodenal atresia, and\nhigh arched palate. (Nelson's 11th ed)",
